[text] # TREM2 binder design — campaign complete

I ran the full de novo mini-binder pipeline (RFdiffusion3 → ProteinMPNN → ESMFold → AF2-multimer) against human TREM2 in one round. The result is a strong set of candidates.

## 1. Target
- **PDB 5UD7**, chain A — wild-type TREM2 Ig-like V domain, X-ray 2.2 Å (Kober et al. 2016, the structure that defined TREM2's basic & hydrophobic surfaces). Chose it over alternatives (6XDS is an MBP fusion; 6Y6C/8T51 carry bound Fabs) for a clean, single-chain, unliganded WT target.
- **Crop 21–129** (109 aa) — the complete IgV ectodomain, gap-free (the 5UD7 gaps are all beyond residue 130). Tight crop → fast RFD3, no contig-spanning-gap errors.

## 2. Target identity
- **UniProt Q9NZC2**, *Homo sapiens* TREM2, full length **230 aa**. Ig-like V-type domain 29–112. Crop sequence verified WT (the `KHW**G**RRK` motif confirms W44/R47 unmutated).

## 3. Hotspots — **A44, A47, A70, A74** (4, structural + literature)
Literature converges on a hydrophobic "CDR" apical groove (binds Aβ/ApoE) adjacent to a basic site (R47/R62, the R47H/R62H Alzheimer's LOF variants). My geometry check (CB distances + exposure) confirmed W44 (exposed CDR1 anchor), R47 (central basic), and the W70/F74 hydrophobic core form one compact, designable face (all within ~13 Å). Used the well-tested CA/CB default atoms.

## 4. Funnel counts
**RFD3 12 backbones** (length 65–95, all came out 93 aa) → **MPNN 48 sequences** (temp 0.1) → **ESMFold 47 survivors** (cut **≥70**; only 1 dropped, mean pLDDT 79.5) → **AF2-multimer 12 complexes**.

*Honest deviation:* I planned 48 AF2 jobs but ESM barely discriminates for helical binders (as expected), and the 4 sequences per backbone are near-identical. I instead ran AF2 on the **best-MPNN representative of each of the 12 backbones** — this answers round-1's real question (which topology docks) and keeps AF2 compute proportionate. A deeper per-backbone sequence sweep is the natural round-2.

## 5. Top 3 designs (ranked by AF2 complex pLDDT; none MSA-degraded)

| Rank | Backbone | Seq preview (first 30 aa) | Monomer pLDDT | **Complex pLDDT** | ipSAE | ipTM | pDockQ |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | m0 | `AAELDARARALAAEALRLLEAGGDPEEVGRL` | 79.4 | **97.2** | 0.78 | 0.88 | 0.50 |
| 2 | m8 | `MKEELVKKAKKLKEEIKKLSEEFVKLAKKYA` | 78.4 | **96.9** | 0.75 | 0.87 | 0.36 |
| 3 | m2 | `AAALLAAAAAAFREAGAIALANWSPEVEAEL` | 82.0 | **96.7** | 0.72 | 0.84 | 0.49 |

All are 93-aa α-helical bundles. Complex PDBs:
- `…/fcd3f2d8bfe3/alphafold2_multimer_0/complex_accdb71dbd_…_model_1_seed_000.pdb`
- `…/fcd3f2d8bfe3/alphafold2_multimer_8/complex_efe92703d1_…_model_1_seed_000.pdb`
- `…/fcd3f2d8bfe3/alphafold2_multimer_2/complex_5f9bbe226f_…_model_1_seed_000.pdb`

**Full ranking:** 11 of 12 backbones cleared all gates (complex pLDDT 88.6–97.2, ipTM 0.75–0.88). Only backbone-11 failed (pLDDT 71, ipSAE 0.13, ipTM 0.42 — dropped).

## 6. MSA-degraded designs
None — every AF2 run used the full ColabFold MMseqs2 MSA (`msa_degraded: false`).

## 7. On-target verification (interface contacts, 4.5 Å)
The top design's epitope centers on the intended groove: **W44** (7 contacts), L69/**W70** (6), L71/L72/M41/N68/**F74**/H67. Ranks 2 and 3 independently land on the same residues, and the best-pDockQ design (m6) contacts all four hotspots including R47. This cross-backbone epitope **consensus** is strong evidence the binders engage the real Aβ/ApoE hydrophobic site, not an artifact.

Top-5 epitope (rank-1): **B44W, B70W, B69L, B71L, B72L**. Top-5 paratope: **A39H, A16L, A32F, A43A, A71L**.

## Calibration footnote
Against the experimentally-validated hit gate (ipSAE ≳ 0.3, complex pLDDT > 80, ipTM > 0.7), **11/12 designs pass all three** — far exceeding the "≥5 with complex pLDDT > 75" success criterion. `ipsae` computed cleanly (no `ipsae_error`). 

Caveats, stated plainly: these are **single-model (`num_models=1`) computational predictions, not experimentally validated**, at exploratory scale (12 backbones vs Bennett 2023's ~10⁴/target). The uniformly high scores across 11 backbones are encouraging but warrant a confirmation pass — re-running the top 5 with `num_models=5` to check ranking variance, and the per-backbone sequence sweep I deferred — before wet-lab. If you want, I can outline that as round 2.

